.TH SDL_ALLOC_SIZE 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_ALLOC_SIZE \- A macro to tag a function as returning a certain allocation.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_begin_code.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_ALLOC_SIZE(p) __attribute__((alloc_size(p)))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This is a hint to the compiler that a function allocates and returns a specific amount of memory based on one of its arguments\[char46] For example, the C runtime\(aqs malloc() function could use this macro with an argument of 1 (first argument to malloc is the size of the allocation)\[char46]
.PP
On compilers without alloc_size support, this is defined to nothing\[char46]
.PP
Most apps don\(aqt need to, and should not, use this directly\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

